  "aliases": ["funk carioca", "brazilian funk", "funk brasileiro", "favela funk"],
  "description": "Baile funk (funk carioca): the sound of the bailes in Rio's favelas at 126 to 136 BPM on the tamborzão: a booming low drum in five uneven hits, rim slaps answering in its gaps, a higher hand drum crossing both and claps on two and four, an 808 following the kick, chopped vocal shouts and horn stabs over a minimal minor vamp, loud, dry and clipped",
  "query": "baile funk beat with booming 808 kicks and congas",
  "alts": ["reggaeton music", "trap beat", "hip hop beat with heavy bass", "dancehall music"],
  "accepted_flaws": ["a distorted clipped recording"],
